# Keep the build context to the handful of files the image actually needs.
#
# Without this the context is ~29 MB — 26 MB of node_modules and 2.2 MB of .git —
# against 136 KB of tracked source. None of it reaches the image (the Dockerfile
# COPYs three named files and runs its own `npm ci`), it is all just uploaded to
# the daemon and discarded.
#
# This matters more than it looks: Glama builds this image in a sandboxed
# microVM to introspect the server, and that build is the gate on the whole
# listing — no build means no tools/list, no recorded schema, and no quality
# score. A context two orders of magnitude larger than it needs to be is pure
# risk for no benefit.
#
# ⚠ node_modules especially: copying a host-built tree into a Linux image is how
# you ship native modules built for the wrong platform. `npm ci` inside the
# image is the only correct source of dependencies.

node_modules/
.git/
.github/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
*.tgz
.DS_Store
